  "term": "ophthalmic nerve",
  "definition": "The ophthalmic nerve is the sensory branch of the fifth cranial nerve. It carries sensory information from the upper face, including the eye, conjunctiva, upper eyelid, upper nose, nasal lining, and scalp.",
